            <ArticleTitle>Aseptic bone necrosis in an amateur scuba diver.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E19</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported that provides further evidence of an old occupational hazard, dysbaric osteonecrosis, presenting in a new population (sports scuba divers) who also appear to be at risk. It highlights the need for an accurate diagnosis of diving related illness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
